# Validation example: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, USE_RI TRUE + CHOLESKY FALSE (dense post-SCF) +
# FUNCTIONAL_POS_CHO_4C TRUE, no MINMAX -- confirms the resolution-of-identity (RI) SCF kernel
# works end to end with the rest of the pipeline (post-SCF MO transform, FUNCTIONAL, ADAM
# FULL_OPTIMIZATION). Compare the DHF electronic energy against lih_gnof_c4_dense_direct.inp's own
# (exact) C4_DHF result -- USE_RI's own approximation should land within ~1e-7 Hartree of it (see
# project memory project-ri-pauto-kr-validation); the post-SCF FULL_OPTIMIZATION numbers then
# follow from whichever (slightly different) converged DHF density/orbitals USE_RI handed it, so
# they are close but not bit-for-bit identical to the dense/SCF_DIRECT_4C examples.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
USE_RI TRUE
FUNCTIONAL_POS_CHO_4C TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
